Mr. Rustam bought a car for his family with a car loan from a bank. The interest rate is fixed in the contract, which means it does not change for the whole term of the loan.

The family's main car-related expenses:
• the loan payment made to the bank every month;
• fuel (methane) costs;
• maintenance: an oil and filter change every 10 000 km, brake pads, tire wear.

The family has now started driving to their dacha and to visit relatives more often than before.
